        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/fjur/{size}/4849_2.png",
        "created_at": "2026-01-27T03:58:35.561Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"LonelyMan\" data-post=\"2\" data-topic=\"32130\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/f4b2a3/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> LonelyMan:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Good start, but even if you’re just writing a single scene, I think it needs more if an ending than it has.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Thanks. Perhaps. Admittedly, I’ve not really any desire to continue it beyond this. As mentioned, it’s just a silly little aping of a Pratchett scene.</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"LonelyMan\" data-post=\"2\" data-topic=\"32130\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/f4b2a3/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> LonelyMan:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Also why is Alpha under the table? She’s usually mostly a person…</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>This, too, is really just due to it being a pastiche of a particular Pratchett scene. That scene includes the character Angua, who’s a werewolf like Alpha, though she often transforms into the shape of a wolf and acts like a dog while doing so, whereas Alpha, I don’t think, ever just turns into a wolf—it seems that she always turns into a wolfish humanoid form.</p>\n<p>Anyways, Alpha’s under the table because Angua was in the scene that I’m aping—I know it’s out of character, but again, it’s a pastiche.</p>",
